WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.580
Speaker 1: Let's go to Chris from Iowa.&nbsp;
Chris, welcome to the program. What is on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:14.880
your mind today? Chris from Iowa, please.
Speaker 2: Can you hear me okay? Yes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:23.160
Wonderful. Okay, So speaking of culture issues,&nbsp;
I think the profession that has been affected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:29.100
the most has been the teaching profession and&nbsp;
education in general. Mm hmm. And so my question&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:38.040
is, how do people who are in the profession&nbsp;
combat that without getting in trouble or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.440
going against the grain? I mean, it seems&nbsp;
like there are times when teachers just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.220
do not have a voice in what's going on.
Speaker 1: So in some sense, it sounds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:52.200
like what you're saying is teaching has become&nbsp;
unbearable for teachers because you've got all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:57.960
these kooks saying, I want to decide what&nbsp;
books and material you're teaching. I want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.260
to decide how you're teaching it. I want to&nbsp;
decide about masks. I want to decide about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:05.040
vaccines. I don't want this. I don't want&nbsp;
that. Is that that's why the teaching has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.920
become so difficult.
Speaker 2:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:16.200
Yeah, it's a lot of outside pressure and noise&nbsp;
and and also it becomes difficult because it feels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:22.260
like we we don't have any really any power to do&nbsp;
anything about it other than keep just keeping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:28.740
our heads down and doing our best. So, dude.
Speaker 1: You're breaking up a little bit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:34.860
Chris. But here's here's the thing, and I hate&nbsp;
that this is the reality. I think that teachers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:41.460
Can't do it on their own. I think teachers&nbsp;
are going to need the support. At minimum,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:48.300
at minimum, of the teachers unions and the&nbsp;
principals and the superintendents and probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:55.080
of local elected officials as well in order&nbsp;
to be able to establish. We're not going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:59.940
be bullied by parents if you show up and act&nbsp;
out at a school board meeting or whatever.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:04.560
You're not going to get your way. That's not&nbsp;
the way to actually have your voice heard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.880
I believe that teachers need to be supported&nbsp;
by all of these different elements. It can't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.780
